WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:06.700
Pain from the past, and stubborn pride, as well as mistakes...

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:13.480
The small wings that stumbled managed to spread out on their own.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:19.940
I’m watching over you, so that all your failures and hesitation will help you tomorrow.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:24.500
So that your stumbles and regrets may someday be treasures.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.200
When we train our hardest every day,
sometimes we need a rest.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.150
Sometimes you need to take a nice break.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:38.010
Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha StrikerS<i>
will now begin.</i>

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.880
Dear Ginny,

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.610
It’s been two weeks since that little incident.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.110
Tia.

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:43.260
It’s morning!

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.120
It’s time to get up!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.930
Tia.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.560
Get up!

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.350
Hey, Tia!

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:58.940
It’s our turn to set up the practice field today.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.900
Get moving!

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.750
So you’re up?

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.960
Why you! I let my guard down for just a second, and you sexually harass me!

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:23.640
It’s just to get us a little closer.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.340
Tia is completely back to normal.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.360
Morning, Caro.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.440
Morning.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:46.240
It’s kind of nice.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.800
Okay, that’s the morning training and the mock battle.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.460
Good work.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:05.740
And just so you know, this was the test
to see if you’ve all cleared the second stage.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.380
What do you think?

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.060
Pass.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.000
That was fast!

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:16.860
Well, after all the practice they’ve done,
it would be a serious issue if they still sucked.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.060
I think you’re all doing well.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.320
Okay then, you’ve cleared the second stage.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.740
Yes!

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:30.160
We’ll take off a stage of your device limiters,
so go see Shari later, okay?

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.620
Tomorrow, we’ll have you start training with the basic forms of your Devices’ second modes.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.510
Yes, ma’am!

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:36.900
Wait... tomorrow?

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.550
Yeah, we’ll start training again tomorrow.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:44.120
We’re supposed to stay on standby at HQ today.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:48.220
Everyone has been training every day since you’ve joined.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.600
So you see...

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.060
You all have the rest of the day off.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.400
Go out to the city and have fun!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.360
Okay!

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.270
That was your entertainment news for the day.

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:11.290
And now for political and economic news.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:15.990
Yesterday at the Bureau’s Surface/Central HQ on Midchilda,

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.580
a budgetary conference for next year was held.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.050
This is the third budget that has been submitted,

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:25.420
and every world is watching carefully due to concerns about taxation issues.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:30.630
The Capital Defense Corps representative,
Lt. General Regius Gaiz,

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:34.080
made an announcement concerning the Bureau’s defensive policies.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:41.280
The advancement and evolution of magic and technology is a wonderful thing.

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:41.900
But!

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.480
This means that the dangers and disasters that face us

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:49.780
are of a scale far greater than they were ten years ago!

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:55.760
Strengthening our weapons is a method to protecting an evolving society!

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:01.620
We do not yet have enough people to adequately defend the capital.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:09.610
If our proposed budget passes,
with a 20% increase in the crime rate,

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:15.390
we can expect a 35% increase in
the arrest rate from the very first year!

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.840
Is that geezer still rambling on about that?

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:23.260
Lt. General Regius has been a hawk for a long time now.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:25.260
Oh, that’s Admiral Midget.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.150
Granny Midget?

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.180
and other serious crimes!

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:33.350
No, it is already in that process.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:37.180
Marshal Kiel and Judicial Advisor Phils are there too.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.610
The renowned Three Admirals are all here.

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.380
But if you look at them now,

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.300
they just look like a bunch of geezers.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.300
You can’t say that, Vita!

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.190
They’re an important group of people!

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:54.080
They’re the ones who took the Bureau from its beginnings to what it is today.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.480
Hey, I <i>like</i> this bunch of geezers.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:02.500
We once accepted a mission to guard them.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:07.320
Admiral Midget seems to like Mistress Hayate and Vita.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:08.720
I see.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:09.780
That makes sense.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.540
I don’t mind loaning it to you, but don’t blow it out.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.070
What kind of protector are you using?

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.620
My own autobarrier.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:28.540
But you know, I watch your training sometimes,
and you’ve changed the way you work lately.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:30.470
Yes.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:35.010
Up until now your movements were the same

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.930
whether you were in a team,
on your own, or in a pair.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:41.870
Lately, you’ve become a lot more adaptable.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:44.860
You’ve started to act more like a center.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:48.110
It’s thanks to everybody’s help.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.060
Okay, it’s looking good.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.010
Here.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:04.330
Thanks.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:12.220
Hey, I’m sorry if I shouldn’t ask this, but...

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:16.800
You were a mage once, right, Sgt. Vice?

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:20.650
Well, I <i>am</i> from the Armed Services.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:24.250
I have just enough experience to give lectures to complete amateurs.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.340
But even so, I’ve always loved helicopters,

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:31.560
so now I’m a pilot.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.640
Your partner’s waiting. Get going.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.410
Thank you!

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.820
You have your handkerchief, right?

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:50.710
Did you remember your I.D. card?

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.980
I’m all set.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.030
Do you have enough money?

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.200
I don’t want you to run out, so...

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:02.600
Fate, I’m getting paid, you know.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.770
Oh... I see.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.720
I’m fine. Thank you.

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:13.190
Well, you’re a boy and two months older than Caro.

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:15.440
So make sure you escort her properly.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:16.990
I will.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:20.990
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.460
You look very pretty, Caro. How cute!

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:27.880
Thank you.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.990
Are those the right size?

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:32.080
Yes, they’re perfect!

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:33.670
Very nice.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:44.350
Well then, make sure you don’t crash.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:45.620
It’s all right.

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:49.680
We rode every day in my old squad.

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:51.840
Tia is a good rider.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:52.260
Okay.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:55.240
I’ll buy you a present, like cookies or something.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:58.350
Thanks, but don’t worry about it.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.200
You two go have fun.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.320
We will.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:02.910
We’re off!

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:13.320
Oh, is the Lightning Squad heading out together?

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:14.560
We’re going now.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:15.710
Okay. Be careful.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:18.540
Come back before dark.

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:20.880
The city is dangerous at night.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:21.640
Okay!

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:42.030
Signum.

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.020
Vita.

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:44.240
Are you heading out?

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:48.210
Yes, to the 108th Battalion and the Church of the Holy King.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:53.670
Major Nakajima is going to make us
a Joint Investigation HQ, so we’re meeting about that.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:55.340
You too, Vita?

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:58.290
I’ll be teaching tactics to their mages.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.530
I never should’ve gotten this teaching credential.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:06.110
If it has to do with the investigation, I should go too.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:07.680
Making preparations is my job.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:11.970
You’re the squad leader, and I’m your adjutant.

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:18.660
Thank you. Are you sure about this?

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:19.470
Do what you want.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:25.960
I’m glad the removing of the first limiters went well.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:26.870
Yes.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:30.480
Starting tomorrow, we’ll be busy adjusting them,

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:34.380
so finishing the adjustments on Nanoha’s and Raising Heart’s unlimited mode,

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:39.160
Exceed Mode, is what I want to work on right now, okay?

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:41.600
And Bardiche’s Zanber Form too.

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:43.830
We’ll be busy.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.600
This is fun!

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:51.500
Oh! We should give you a complete check-up while we’re at it, Command Sergeant Major Rein.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.510
That’s right.

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:55.250
If you please.

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.070
Roger that.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:03.570
You haven’t needed to enter Unison with anybody lately, right?

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:11.340
No. Neither Hayate, Signum, nor Vita have needed to use me.

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:14.520
That’s a good thing in and of itself, right?

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:18.420
But I need to be ready to live up to my name,

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:22.400
Reinforce, the Wind of Blessing,

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:32.620
so take care of my check-up,
and check the Book of the Azure Sky, Shari.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:33.330
Okay.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.210
This is fun!

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:00.710
Hold on tight!

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.130
I’m fine!

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:07.990
The weather’s nice.
This is a great day for riding a motorcycle.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:11.520
Yeah, I just want to keep going on forever.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:15.540
We can do something else if you want,
but we’re having fun in town first, right?

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:19.980
For now, let’s go to town, get some ice cream, and then decide what else.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:21.280
Sure, sure.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:22.900
Okay, I’m going to gun it!

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:37.160
The plan for today that Shari made for us...

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:45.050
starts with going to Third Avenue via railway,
walking around the city together,

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:48.760
and enjoying window shopping and conversation.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:53.580
Then we’re to eat in a place with
an atmosphere conducive to conversation.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:57.020
I pray for your success.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.100
T-This seems kind of hard.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:04.020
For now, let’s just go with what she planned.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.010
Sure!

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:10.870
By the way, Caro, you have
another dragon besides Fried, right?

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:15.070
Yes, Voltaire. He’s an immense black dragon.

00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:22.290
I raised Fried from an egg, but Voltaire is
an ancient guardian dragon of the world of Alzus.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:29.250
So it’s more that I’m Voltaire’s priestess and that he’s lending me power than that he’s my dragon.

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:30.720
It’s something like that.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:35.740
I see. It would be nice if you could introduce him to me like Fried.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.200
But if he’s that important of a dragon,

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:40.690
then I guess you can’t just bring him here for me to say hello to him.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:48.070
Yeah. He’s very large, and I can only borrow his power when I really need it.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:51.490
But I’ll be sure to introduce you to him someday.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:57.000
And it seems that Fried thinks of you as a real friend, Erio.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.220
That’s good.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:01.920
I’m sure Voltaire will like you.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:06.370
Third Avenue South Exit.

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:10.140
To get to Outer Gateway, please use platforms 9 to 12.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:15.870
To get to the Fairway, please use platforms 7 and 8.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:30.020
The ice cream here looks really awesome!

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:31.730
Thanks.

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:33.910
You really like ice cream!

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:36.700
’Cause it’s so yummy! Mmm... ice cream!

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.480
Okay then.

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.790
Cheers!

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:52.330
Once we eat our ice cream, let’s go to the arcade.

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:55.050
Good idea! We haven’t been there in a long time.

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:57.100
This is really nice once in a while, isn’t it?

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:58.020
It is!

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:05.520
Hayate, look who’s back!

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.000
Welcome back.

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:09.760
Did you get a check-up?

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:10.680
Yes indeedy.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:13.170
A full check of me and the Book of the Azure Sky.

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:13.950
I see.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:19.910
Shari is going to come and take your
Book of the Night Sky and Schwertkreuz later.

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:22.330
Roger.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:34.710
I hope we can spend the day resting.

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:35.720
Yes indeedy.

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:45.330
We really are taking it easy.

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:48.440
Don’t do that.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:57.910
Caro, did you spend your breaks
like this before you came to Riot Force 6?

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.540
Actually, not really.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:05.460
But Fate took me to amusement parks
and aquariums sometimes.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.940
Really? Me too!

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:13.470
The first time she took me to
an amusement park, it was really fun.

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:15.170
Too fun.

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:20.360
When the sun went down
and my funtime was over, I was so sad.

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:22.240
I cried just a bit.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.770
I can understand that.

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.500
The day before, you’re looking forward to it so much you can’t sleep,

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:30.730
and when it’s over, you’re just so sad.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:32.650
Yes! That’s exactly it!

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:40.400
I understand that. But Fate was really busy
and still found time to look after me.

00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:46.240
Yes.

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:48.000
This is Lightning 3.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.320
Hi! This is Stars 3.

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.200
How’s your day off?

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:53.920
Having fun?

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:54.750
Yes,

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:57.520
even though we just got started.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:18:02.000
We were wondering if you were having any problems.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.350
Thank you!

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:06.170
Anyway, we’re fine.

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:07.770
What are you doing?

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:13.210
Well, we’re at the park as planned,
and then we’re going to a department store.

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:14.140
That’s what we’re doing.

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:17.600
After that, we’ll eat and see a movie,

00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:21.320
and then we’ll go to the coastline and watch the sunset this evening.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:23.030
That’s the plan they made for us.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:26.750
We’re going to clear them all in order.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.300
“Clear”? Those kids!

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:31.710
Well, it’s healthy.

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:35.440
No, don’t worry about it.

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:38.290
Okay, if anything comes up,

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:40.040
give us a call.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:43.130
We’re senior to you in terms of hanging out in town too.

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:44.000
Great!

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.220
Thank you!

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:47.910
Later.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:52.180
Subaru and Tia are nice.

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:53.600
They are!

00:18:59.350 --> 00:19:02.930
But it really has been a long time since we’ve relaxed this much.

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:04.150
Hasn’t it.

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:04.640
Here.

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:12.280
I hope there aren’t any crimes or accidents or anything.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:13.440
Yeah.

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:24.840
Sergeant Ginga Nakajima,
with the Ground Armed Service’s 108th Battalion

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:27.680
I’ve come to help investigate the scene.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.260
Thank you.

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:31.350
I heard that it was a rollover accident.

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:34.360
Yes, but the circumstances of the rollover were strange.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:40.740
Furthermore, the driver is in a state of total shock.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:44.160
It seems he was attacked by something,
and then his cargo blew up.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:47.820
All he was carrying were bottled drinks and canned goods.

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:50.080
Nothing that explodes.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:54.040
And there is something strange down there.

00:20:10.090 --> 00:20:12.810
Is this a life pod?

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:19.080
The six Type 1 Drones that were following the Relic signature have all been destroyed.

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:23.000
Oh my. Was it a Bureau mage who took them out?

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:25.330
Or did we get lucky?

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:29.460
I can’t say for sure, but it seems to be the latter.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:31.300
Splendid.

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:33.710
I’ll chase after it immediately.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:37.120
Hey, Doctor,

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.240
I’d like to go, then.

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:41.590
Nove, you would?

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:42.910
No, Nove.

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:45.760
Your weapons are still being adjusted.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:50.570
If we did get lucky this time,
then I want to see for myself.

00:20:50.570 --> 00:20:53.230
There’s no need to hurry.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:57.690
It will certainly come here sometime.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:01.850
For now, I’d like you to just wait.

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:03.070
Understood?

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:05.030
I understand.

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:09.900
Let’s launch the Drones once we get a better handle on the situation.

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:13.790
I’ll find somebody suitable from my younger sisters.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:19.960
Sure, and while I’m at it, I’ll ask my dear friend.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:25.340
My sweet Lutecia, can you hear me?

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.500
This has to do with a Relic.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:30.690
Can you help me out a bit?

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:49.370
I have to go.

00:21:58.670 --> 00:21:59.640
Erio?

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:02.620
Caro, did you hear something?

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:03.830
Like what?

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:06.100
It was like grinding or something.

00:22:24.350 --> 00:22:26.700
An alert to everyone from Caro?

00:22:28.600 --> 00:22:30.280
What is it, I wonder.

00:22:30.280 --> 00:22:33.000
This is Lightning 4!

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:36.250
We have an emergency situation. I will report.

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:42.170
We’ve found a case believed to be a Relic
in a back alley at F23 Third Avenue.

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:46.090
There is a girl who we believe was carrying the case.

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:48.280
The girl is unconscious.

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:49.540
Give us orders, please.

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:55.300
Subaru, Teana, I’m sorry,
but your break is cancelled.

00:22:55.300 --> 00:22:56.050
Yes, ma’am!

00:22:56.050 --> 00:22:56.890
It’s okay.

00:22:56.890 --> 00:22:59.040
We’ll get medical assistance ready.

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:01.860
You two secure the girl and the case.

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:03.900
Give her first aid.

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:04.520
Yes, ma’am!

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:06.600
All staff on standby.

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:09.490
Anybody who isn’t at their post, return to it.

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:10.530
Yes, ma’am!

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:14.440
Recover the girl and the Relic safely and securely.

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:15.700
Roger.

00:25:17.470 --> 00:25:19.330
A girl
brought a Relic to us.

00:25:19.330 --> 00:25:21.330
An incident
began to take shape.

00:25:21.330 --> 00:25:24.040
Battles will be fought on the ground and in the sky.

00:25:32.450 --> 00:25:34.970
Toward the sky, I too will take off!
